
---
---

<dialog class="info-dialog" id="service-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="service-dialog-title">
  <div class="info-dialog__shell">
    <header class="info-dialog__head">
      <p class="note note--accent" id="service-dialog-kicker" hidden></p>
      <button class="info-dialog__close" type="button" data-dialog-close aria-label="Close"><svg class="ui-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="/img/ui-icons.svg#close"></use></svg></button>
    </header>

    <div class="info-dialog__content" tabindex="0" data-lenis-prevent data-lenis-prevent-touch data-lenis-prevent-wheel>
      <h2 class="h1 info-dialog__title" id="service-dialog-title">Services</h2>
      <div id="service-dialog-body"></div>
    </div>

    <footer class="info-dialog__foot">
      <span class="note">Fees are in GBP. If you need the invoice in another currency, I will confirm that amount before work starts.</span>

    </footer>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog class="info-dialog" id="policy-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="policy-dialog-title">
  <div class="info-dialog__shell">
    <header class="info-dialog__head">
      <p class="note note--accent">Terms and conditions</p>
      <button class="info-dialog__close" type="button" data-dialog-close aria-label="Close"><svg class="ui-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="/img/ui-icons.svg#close"></use></svg></button>
    </header>

    <div class="info-dialog__content" tabindex="0" data-lenis-prevent data-lenis-prevent-touch data-lenis-prevent-wheel>
      <h2 class="h1 info-dialog__title" id="policy-dialog-title">Terms and conditions</h2>
      <p class="info-dialog__intro">How I work, how payment works and what to expect before a project begins. The scope and deliverables for each project are confirmed in the agreed brief.</p>

      <section class="policy-group">
        <p class="note note--accent">01 / BOOKING & PAYMENT</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Secure the slot</h3>
        <p>A 50% non-refundable deposit of the total project fee reserves your slot. I start when the deposit clears: no research, sketches or mood boards before then.</p>
        <p>The remaining 50% is due when you approve the final artwork, before I send the final files.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-group">
        <p class="note note--accent">02 / REVISIONS</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Keep feedback within scope</h3>
        <p>Each project includes an agreed number of revision rounds, confirmed in your brief. A round is one consolidated set of changes, sent together. Extra rounds, and changes that go against the approved brief, are £60 per round.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-group">
        <p class="note note--accent">03 / RUSH WORK</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Accelerated timelines</h3>
        <p>If you need delivery less than 72 hours after the deposit has cleared and the brief is agreed, a 30% premium applies to the base quote, and the project is paid 100% upfront.</p>
        <p>Messages or feedback sent at a weekend or outside working hours don't count as rush work.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-group">
        <p class="note note--accent">04 / CANCELLATION</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Project termination</h3>
        <p>If you pause or cancel a project, I keep the 50% deposit. If you cancel after I have sent you the second set of layouts, the total due is 75% of the project fee.</p>
        <p>For example, on a £1,000 project, the deposit is £500, and if you cancel after the second set of layouts you pay a further £250: £750 in total.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-group">
        <p class="note note--accent">05 / USAGE & INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Final files and usage rights</h3>
        <p>Once the invoice is paid in full, you can use the final files listed in your brief, in the formats listed, for ongoing print and digital use. Unused concepts and drafts stay mine.</p>
        <p>Layered or editable working files are included only if your brief says so. Reselling or redistributing the artwork, using it in markets beyond those agreed, or selling it directly as a product (for example as prints or merchandise) needs a separate licence agreed with me.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-group">
        <p class="note note--accent">06 / SIGNAGE & PRODUCTION</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Production requirements</h3>
        <p>Signage work needs final engineering blueprints from you before I start designing. Changes of scale requested after the brief are £120 each.</p>
        <p>A site visit is £175. It covers supervising installation, evaluating a site or supporting your production vendors.</p>
        
      </section>

      <section class="policy-group">
        <p class="note note--accent">07 / MONTHLY SOCIAL MEDIA</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Retainer commitment</h3>
        <p>The monthly social media retainer has a three-month minimum. 50% of each month's fee must clear before that month's work begins.</p>
      </section>

      <p class="policy-note">These terms are a summary. Scope, deliverables, timelines, licensing and charges are confirmed in writing before work begins.</p>
    </div>

    <footer class="info-dialog__foot">
      <span class="note">Fees are in GBP. If you need the invoice in another currency, I will confirm that amount before work starts.</span>

    </footer>
  </div>
</dialog>

<script>
  const serviceDialog = document.querySelector("#service-dialog");
  const policyDialog = document.querySelector("#policy-dialog");
  const serviceTitle = document.querySelector("#service-dialog-title");
  const serviceKicker = document.querySelector("#service-dialog-kicker");
  const serviceBody = document.querySelector("#service-dialog-body");
  const dialogOpeners = new WeakMap();

  const services = {
    campaign: {
      title: "Campaign systems",
      content: `
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Event identity & visual direction</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">Quoted per brief</p>
          <p>Visual themes and art direction developed into a consistent campaign across editorial covers, event print, social media and merchandise. From initial visual directions to final artwork, the design stays recognisable across formats and audiences.</p>
          <p class="note">VISUAL DIRECTION · KEY ART · EDITORIAL & PRINT · MERCHANDISE</p>
        </section>
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Sports & ticket-promotion campaigns</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">Quoted per brief</p>
          <p>Fixture announcements, match-day graphics, banners, posters and promotional reels designed as a connected series. Creative can be adapted for different matches, announcements and ticket-promotion messages while keeping the campaign consistent.</p>
          <p class="note">SOCIAL CAMPAIGNS · MATCH-DAY ASSETS · BANNERS · PROMOTIONAL REELS</p>
        </section>
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Event launches & ongoing promotion</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">Quoted per brief</p>
          <p>Campaign assets from pre-event teasers and sneak peeks to launch announcements, printed materials and post-event highlights. Designed to build anticipation beforehand and document the event afterwards across social, video, print and merchandise.</p>
          <p class="note">TEASERS · LAUNCH CONTENT · PRINT COLLATERAL · POST-EVENT HIGHLIGHTS</p>
        </section>`
    },
    identity: {
      title: "Identity & Branding Systems",
      content: `
        <section class="rate-item">
          <p class="note note--accent">CORPORATE & BUSINESS</p>
          <h3 class="h3">Brand identity package</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">£1,500–£3,000</p>
          <p>Primary logo, responsive secondary layouts, brand iconography, typography hierarchy, HEX/RGB/CMYK colour specifications, a multi-page brand style guide and print-ready business cards, letterheads and email signatures.</p>
          <p class="note">14–21 BUSINESS DAYS · 3 INITIAL DIRECTIONS · UP TO 4 REVISION ROUNDS</p>
        </section>
        <section class="rate-item">
          <p class="note note--accent">WEDDINGS & PERSONAL IDENTITY</p>
          <h3 class="h3">Wedding logo & monogram suite</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">£150–£300</p>
          <p>Custom initials or vector illustrations, master vector layouts (.AI, .EPS) and press-ready PDFs for printing, stamping or embroidery.</p>
          <p class="note">5–7 BUSINESS DAYS · 3 INITIAL CONCEPTS · UP TO 2 REVISION ROUNDS</p>
        </section>
        
        `
    },
    media: {
      title: "Media, Publishing & Spatial Graphics",
      content: `
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Large-scale print & signage</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">£350–£850 <span>per structural asset</span></p>
          <p>Environmental graphics for arches, event backdrops, architectural signage and wraps; 1:1 high-resolution production files, bleed and crop alignment, and material recommendations for vinyl, ACP, acrylic or canvas.</p>
          <p class="note">7–12 BUSINESS DAYS · 2 VARIATIONS · UP TO 3 REVISION ROUNDS</p>
        </section>
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Book cover design</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">£200–£450</p>
          <p>Full print jacket including front, spine, back and space for flap copy, plus screen-ready JPG/PNG e-book cover exports.</p>
          <p class="note">7–10 BUSINESS DAYS · 2 TYPOGRAPHIC LAYOUTS · UP TO 3 REVISION ROUNDS</p>
        </section>
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Album cover design</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">£120–£250</p>
          <p>3000 × 3000 px digital artwork for music platforms, plus one matching social announcement template or static canvas backdrop.</p>
          <p class="note">5–7 BUSINESS DAYS · 2 INITIAL CONCEPTS · UP TO 2 REVISION ROUNDS</p>
        </section>
        
        `
    },
    artwork: {
      title: "Artwork & Marketing",
      content: `
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Monthly social media retainer</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">Quoted per brief</p>
          <p>A monthly batch of 12–15 custom static layouts or multi-frame carousel posts, matching covers and promotional frames, plus organised Canva setups or Photoshop master assets.</p>
          <p class="note">MINIMUM 3-MONTH COMMITMENT · 50% RETAINER BEFORE EACH MONTH'S WORK BEGINS</p>
        </section>
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Personalised digital illustrations</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">£100–£250 <span>per layout</span></p>
          <p>Custom vector or digital-painting artwork and portraits for digital gifting or merchandise. Commercial retail usage requires a separate rights add-on.</p>
          <p class="note">5–8 BUSINESS DAYS · 1 ROUGH DRAFT · UP TO 2 REVISION ROUNDS</p>
        </section>
        <section class="rate-item">
          <h3 class="h3">Posters & collateral</h3>
          <p class="rate-price">£80–£200 <span>per asset</span></p>
          <p>Single visual assets in a tailored visual style, with print-ready PDF and digital PNG exports.</p>
          <p class="note">3–5 BUSINESS DAYS · 1 MAIN LAYOUT · UP TO 2 REVISION ROUNDS</p>
        </section>
        
        `
    },
    custom: {
      title: "Custom Requests",
      content: `
        <p class="info-dialog__intro">If your brief combines multiple services or needs something not listed in the rate card, send the intended outcome, deliverables, timeline and any production requirements. I'll review the scope and confirm a quote before work begins.</p>
        <p class="note">CUSTOM PROJECTS ARE QUOTED ACCORDING TO SCOPE.</p>`
    }
  };

function resetDialogScroll(dialog) {
  const content = dialog.querySelector(".info-dialog__content");

  if (content) {
    content.scrollTop = 0;
    content.scrollTo(0, 0);
  }
}

function openInfoDialog(dialog, opener) {
  if (!(dialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement)) return;

  if (opener instanceof HTMLElement) dialogOpeners.set(dialog, opener);
  if (window.__lenis) window.__lenis.stop();

  dialog.showModal();
  resetDialogScroll(dialog);

  requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    resetDialogScroll(dialog);
    dialog.querySelector("[data-dialog-close]")?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
  });
}
function closeDialog(dialog) {
  if (dialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement && dialog.open) {
    dialog.close();
  }
}

  document.querySelectorAll("[data-service-open]").forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const key = button.getAttribute("data-service-open");
      const item = services[key];
      if (!item || !(serviceDialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement)) return;

      serviceKicker.textContent = "";
      serviceKicker.hidden = true;
      serviceTitle.textContent = item.title || "Services";
      serviceBody.innerHTML = item.content;
      openInfoDialog(serviceDialog, button);
    });
  });

 document.querySelectorAll("[data-policy-open]").forEach((button) => {
  button.addEventListener("click", () => {
    if (policyDialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement) {
      openInfoDialog(policyDialog, button);
    }
  });
});

  // Open the existing rates/terms dialog from the shared footer on any page.
  const ratesFooterLinks = document.querySelectorAll('a[href="/?rates=terms#services"]');
  ratesFooterLinks.forEach((link) => {
    link.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      openInfoDialog(policyDialog, link);
    });
  });

  if (new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get("rates") === "terms") {
    openInfoDialog(policyDialog);
    window.history.replaceState(null, "", window.location.pathname + window.location.hash);
  }

  document.querySelectorAll("[data-dialog-close]").forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener("click", () => {
      closeDialog(button.closest("dialog"));
    });
  });
  

[serviceDialog, policyDialog].forEach((dialog) => {
  if (!(dialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement)) return;
  // Let the dialog handle its own mouse-wheel scrolling.
  dialog.addEventListener("wheel", (event) => {
    event.stopPropagation();
  }, { passive: true });
  dialog.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
    if (event.target === dialog) dialog.close();
  });

  dialog.addEventListener("close", () => {
  // Clear the previous scroll position before this dialog is reopened.
  resetDialogScroll(dialog);


  // Resume normal page scrolling after the window closes.
  if (window.__lenis) window.__lenis.start();
  const opener = dialogOpeners.get(dialog);
  if (opener?.isConnected) opener.focus({ preventScroll: true });
});
});

  
</script>
